skill: "moderation-escalation-ladder"
sections[3]:
  - "# moderation-escalation-ladder\n\nEnforce the moderation ladder consistently across channels: policy classes, escalating actions, evidence snapshots, appeals and the weekly false-positive review. Use when a violation is reported or detected, when an appeal arrives, or when moderation stats are due for the transparency report.\n\nOwner: role-community-manager (pod-customer, marketing). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"moderation policy moderation-policy.toon (classes, ladder, appeal window); report queue and automod flags; member history; channel config for discord-automation and slack-automation\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/community/moderation-log.toon with case evidence[] and action; strike-ledger.toon per member; appeals register; transparency-report data block\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load moderation-policy.toon and fix its version; every action taken this period is judged against that version, including for conduct before it.\n2. Classify each flagged item into a policy class (spam, harassment, scam, misinfo, off-platform risk); classification cites the clause, not the moderator's mood.\n3. Snapshot evidence before any action: message content, context window, member history reference; action without prior evidence is reverted, not defended.\n4. Apply the ladder per strike count and severity: warn, mute, suspend, ban; skipping steps requires a severity class that the policy explicitly marks as skip-capable.\n5. Route borderline cases to the human review list instead of guessing; the automation's uncertainty is logged with the item, and the queue is worked in order.\n6. Process appeals within the policy window; an appeal re-opens the case file, not a new one, and the outcome cites the policy clause either way.\n7. Run the weekly false-positive review over automod flags that were reversed; tune the automod rules only through a recorded change note, never silently.\n8. Write moderation-log.toon and strike-ledger.toon; assemble the transparency report data (actions by class, appeal outcomes) and emit ask_question for any ban beyond the automatic class.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nbans beyond automatic class to operator; automod tuning notes to channel automation owners.\n"
